WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:02.910
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood.

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:03.743
- No.

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.667
No, I can't, no.

00:00:07.837 --> 00:00:09.557
- [Mark] Why not?

00:00:09.557 --> 00:00:10.390
- No, I'm good.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:13.443
I'm good.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.541
- [Mark] Do you talk to your family?

00:00:19.541 --> 00:00:20.374
- No.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.347
- [Mark] Do you have kids?

00:00:25.347 --> 00:00:29.830
- No.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.006
- [Mark] Do you have an
abscess on your left arm?

00:00:32.006 --> 00:00:32.839
- Yeah.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:39.813
- [Mark] Okay.

00:00:41.528 --> 00:00:43.445
We're not getting much.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.720
All right, so TJ.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.050
- Yep.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:04.090
- [Mark] Where are you from originally?

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:05.590
- I'm from Ohio,

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:06.880
a small town.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.030
- [Mark] How long have you been out here?

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:11.045
- Two and 1/2, three years.

00:01:11.045 --> 00:01:13.720
- [Mark] What brought you out here?

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.720
- Well, the guy I was with,

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.620
we caught a case in Ohio,

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:20.130
and he got out and came down here,

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.320
so I followed him.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:24.060
Plus the drugs are easy here, yeah.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.980
- [Mark] So that was possession in Ohio?

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:26.863
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:30.163
- [Mark] And where are
you sleeping out here?

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:32.933
Wherever.

00:01:32.933 --> 00:01:34.543
- Yeah, usually tent to tent,

00:01:35.682 --> 00:01:37.643
I had one, but.
- [Mark] You look pretty clean

00:01:37.643 --> 00:01:39.140
for somebody who's going tent to tent.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.741
- Yeah, I try not to
look like the people--

00:01:40.741 --> 00:01:41.574
- [Mark] You don't.

00:01:41.574 --> 00:01:42.500
- Yeah.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.200
It's easy not to look like that.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.110
- [Mark] Well, you got the showers down.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:48.800
- Yeah, it's like,

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.200
go get up and take a shower.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:54.132
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood,

00:01:54.132 --> 00:01:56.965
what did your childhood look like?

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:02.860
- Okay, so, pretty much growing up,

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.480
it was just me for a little bit,

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:08.130
and then my mom got
pregnant with my brother.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.940
And my stepdad was the biggest coke dealer

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:11.950
in our small town,

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.730
so we had everything we wanted

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:17.184
but the cops were always
raiding our place.

00:02:17.184 --> 00:02:19.710
They'd throw in the flash bombs

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:20.850
and everything would be all bright,

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:21.683
we couldn't see shit,

00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:23.880
and then our stepdad, my dad,

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.310
his dad was on the floor,

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:27.140
arrested and shit.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.370
And then we went through
that for like six years,

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.840
and my mom was a big alcoholic

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.743
so she used to beat me all the time.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.480
Pretty much I started raising my brother

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.870
because she quit paying attention to us.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:43.810
- [Mark] You started what your brother?

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:44.643
- Raising my brother.

00:02:44.643 --> 00:02:45.708
- [Mark] Oh, raising your brother.

00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:48.410
- Yeah, and so my mom,

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:51.150
there'd be different guys in and out.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.830
And some of them,

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:55.770
a couple of times they kinda started,

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:56.603
they would hit on me,

00:02:56.603 --> 00:02:58.280
and when I started getting older.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.060
And a couple,

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.100
one time I woke up

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.690
and one of my mom's boyfriends

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.790
was in the bed with me and shit,

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:08.126
and that was weird, you know what I mean?

00:03:08.126 --> 00:03:09.120
- [Mark] How old were you then?

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.700
- Probably 13, yeah.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.180
And then my mom got back with my stepdad

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.840
after he got out of prison,

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:20.090
and shit started getting weird then too.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:23.890
I caught him filming me
when I was taking a shower,

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.010
shit like that.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:25.950
And that fucked me up

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.813
because that was supposed to be my dad.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.370
My real dad lives in Pennsylvania,

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.240
he's cool and all,

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.480
but I don't know,

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:35.713
I don't talk to him.

00:03:35.713 --> 00:03:37.720
My mom just died two years ago,

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.750
she OD'ed on heroin,

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:40.760
but she didn't even do heroin,

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.763
so her boyfriend got
involuntary manslaughter.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:50.503
My brother's 19 now,

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:52.733
I don't really know,

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.180
my childhood was just fucked up,

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:57.900
that my house was a party house.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.030
Everybody came there to party,

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:00.080
you know what I mean?

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:03.760
Growing up, I had to clean up needles

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.677
and I had to clean up beer
bottles and shit like that,

00:04:05.677 --> 00:04:08.850
you know what I mean, so?
- [Mark] How old are you?

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.500
- [TJ] I just turned 25 in April.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.100
I don't know.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.463
- [Mark] What do you do for money?

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.205
- [TJ] See guys.

00:04:19.205 --> 00:04:21.009
- [Mark] Yeah, that's
typically over the night,

00:04:21.009 --> 00:04:21.920
during the night?

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:23.850
- [TJ] Yeah, because the daytime's slow.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.417
You know what I mean?

00:04:25.417 --> 00:04:26.717
But when I first got here,

00:04:29.164 --> 00:04:31.610
I look better now than what I did

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:33.530
because I was strung out,

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:35.040
but I had guys driving up to me,

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.647
offering me $5 to fuck and shit.

00:04:38.647 --> 00:04:40.177
And I was like,

00:04:40.177 --> 00:04:41.140
"Yeah, sure, okay,"

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:41.973
get in the car,

00:04:41.973 --> 00:04:42.873
take the $5, get out.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:45.453
Shit like that.

00:04:45.453 --> 00:04:47.733
This place is very cheap.

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.603
- [Mark] Where would you like
to see yourself in five years?

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:57.510
- [TJ] I always wanted to be a mom,

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:59.413
a stay at home mom,

00:04:59.413 --> 00:05:00.540
but a good mom.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.700
I always wanted to be better than my mom,

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.733
you know what I mean?

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:06.413
Yeah.

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:09.580
I don't see myself here.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:10.990
- [Mark] Yeah, well, you're
still young and beautiful,

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:12.060
you could make that happen.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:13.460
- [TJ] I mean, if I
don't end up doing that,

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:15.240
I'll probably be dead,

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.293
because the dope.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:18.610
- [Mark] Look around at some of the women

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:19.680
that are older that have been here.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:20.513
- Yeah, but some of them,

00:05:20.513 --> 00:05:21.590
you look around and they look older,

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:22.820
but they're really not.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:24.450
- [Mark] Well, that's what I'm saying,

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:25.480
that's what I'm saying.

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:26.340
- Yeah.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.408
- [Mark] You hang out here long enough,

00:05:27.408 --> 00:05:28.600
eventually it takes a toll.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.853
- Yeah, because sometimes I can't get up

00:05:30.853 --> 00:05:33.220
because my back's hurting
and my knees are hurting

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.233
and shit like that,

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:35.066
I ain't never felt that,

00:05:35.066 --> 00:05:36.520
I've been doing dope for seven years.

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:40.454
This dope is bad down here.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:43.700
It's giving me holes in my skin and shit,

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:45.183
it's weird, but.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.430
- [Mark] Is it heroin
that makes your skin.

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:50.928
- Yeah, yeah, it's the heroin.

00:05:50.928 --> 00:05:52.360
And now they got fentanyl,

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:54.340
and that's what my mom and
my brother died off of,

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:55.173
my big brother.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.226
- [Mark] Is there fentanyl in
the heroin that you're doing?

00:05:58.226 --> 00:05:59.497
- Yeah, because they,

00:05:59.497 --> 00:06:00.850
and it's everywhere,

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:02.896
you can't even get a batch of
heroin without fentanyl in it.

00:06:02.896 --> 00:06:03.729
- [Mark] Oh, is that right.

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.580
- Yeah, they got test strips
down at the needle exchange,

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.730
you put it in the cooker
when you're done cooking up.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:08.563
You just stick it in there

00:06:08.563 --> 00:06:10.058
and it'll tell you how
much fentanyl's in it.

00:06:10.058 --> 00:06:11.753
- [Mark] Oh right.

00:06:11.753 --> 00:06:13.420
- Yeah, pretty much.

00:06:16.186 --> 00:06:17.019
Shit.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.433
I don't even know what else to say.

00:06:22.356 --> 00:06:23.189
I got more to say,

00:06:23.189 --> 00:06:26.257
but it's gotta be,

00:06:26.257 --> 00:06:27.090
I have more to say,

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:29.950
but I've got a problem with,

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.740
I bounce back and forward from
different parts of my life

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:33.860
because stuff just comes up, oh,

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.020
like this happened and that happened,

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.062
because that's what really happened.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:39.130
But it don't make sense

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:44.130
because I go from 12 to
18 to 15 years old and,

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:46.450
you know what I mean?

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:48.880
I guess that's just my ADD.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.943
But I don't know.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:53.030
I think probably living in the projects

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:54.370
was the hardest when I was growing up

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:58.050
because my mom was really
bad drinking there,

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.040
and drinking,

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:01.300
and that's when all the
guys would come over

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:02.133
and shit like that,

00:07:02.133 --> 00:07:04.010
that's when they all
started first coming over.

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:06.513
So and my mom would,

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.490
I'd have to get my brother up for school,

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:10.630
I'd miss my bus usually.

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:14.680
My mom cracked three of my
ribs one time kicking me

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.040
because I kicked my bus one time

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:18.190
so she had to get up
and take me to school.

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:21.160
And that's when children
services started coming in,

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:23.840
but I'd always clean
the house up real quick,

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:27.780
do you know what I mean? And
so we wouldn't get taken away.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.200
But I ended up getting taken away anyways

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:32.530
because I was a bad kid, I guess.

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:35.503
And I got put in 21
different foster homes,

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:38.223
I was in and out of juvie.

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:41.580
- [Mark] What age were
you when you left home?

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:43.433
- 14, yeah.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:50.363
Yeah, my brother got to stay with his dad,

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:56.050
and I got put in the system, so.

00:07:58.383 --> 00:07:59.813
- [Mark] Did you go to jail?

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:02.213
- Yeah, oh yeah.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:04.690
- [Mark] How many times?

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:06.803
- I can't even tell you, too many.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:14.319
- [Mark] What's the hardest
part about living down here?

00:08:14.319 --> 00:08:15.569
- Hardest part,

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:22.340
probably the bullshit that
you go through with the men.

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:26.973
Probably that, probably
because everybody wants,

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:28.663
you know what I mean?

00:08:28.663 --> 00:08:30.190
If you're white and you're cute,

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:31.690
everybody wants a part of you,

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:34.947
a piece of you, everybody wants.

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:37.394
"TJ, TJ, hey, over here."

00:08:37.394 --> 00:08:39.560
It doesn't matter how many
times I've seen them a day,

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:43.460
it doesn't matter if I've been
at their tent for two hours,

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:44.293
you know what I mean,

00:08:44.293 --> 00:08:45.126
they're still yelling my name

00:08:45.126 --> 00:08:47.200
if I fucking just leave their tent.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:51.327
It's crazy.

00:08:51.327 --> 00:08:52.160
- [Mark] You've had
some crazy stuff happen

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:53.680
with guys that pick you up?

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:54.513
- Yeah.

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:00.660
Twice, one time,

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:03.442
this guy picked me up in his truck

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:06.220
and he chocked me out

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:08.680
and he raped me or whatever.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:10.520
But the crazy part was

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:13.230
was he kept passing by the tent everyday

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.810
and he'd just wave at me,

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:17.320
me and my dude. My dude, I
didn't tell my dude who he was

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:20.650
because I don't know
why I didn't tell him.

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:21.650
But I told him afterwards,

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:23.150
after we moved somewhere else,

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.310
but that was fucked up

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:28.030
because I'd see him everyday afterwards,

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:30.310
do you know what I mean? Because
he made sure I'd see him.

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:35.140
The hardest thing that
probably ever happened to me

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:36.740
was when I got kidnapped in Ohio

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:42.670
because I was fighting with
my boyfriend at the time

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:46.320
and it was an alcohol date,

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:47.350
and I don't usually do alcohols,

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.450
which means you go,

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:51.650
you leave your spot to go to their spot.

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:54.690
But I did because I was
mad at my boyfriend,

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:57.160
and I was texting him while
I was getting in the car

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:57.993
and everything like that.

00:09:57.993 --> 00:10:00.170
And so, I wasn't paying
attention to the guy driving,

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:02.380
and we started going out the parking lot,

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:04.047
my boyfriend even crossed
past us and was like,

00:10:04.047 --> 00:10:04.880
"What are you doing?

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:05.870
"Where are you going?"

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:08.130
And I was like, "Fuck you," whatever.

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:10.370
Well, an hour away,

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:11.203
the dude was like,

00:10:11.203 --> 00:10:13.017
"Oh, by the way, "we can't
go to my house anymore,

00:10:13.017 --> 00:10:13.850
"my roommate's there."

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:15.590
And started taking me to the woods.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:16.660
So then I say to my boyfriend,

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:17.493
I was like, "Okay,

00:10:17.493 --> 00:10:18.326
"something's going on,

00:10:18.326 --> 00:10:19.487
"I'm going to the woods now."

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:21.270
And he started calling,

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:22.450
and the dude grabbed my cellphone

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:23.670
and smashed it up against the windshield

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:25.358
so the battery fell out.

00:10:25.358 --> 00:10:27.180
(siren wailing)

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:29.053
You hear that all day long.

00:10:29.053 --> 00:10:29.886
- [Mark] All night long.

00:10:29.886 --> 00:10:31.490
- All night long.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:34.380
So anyways, when I tried
to jump out the car,

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:35.213
he jumped on top of me

00:10:35.213 --> 00:10:38.101
and he punched me and
dragged me back into the car.

00:10:38.101 --> 00:10:39.720
And he did whatever,

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:41.000
I mean, he did whatever,

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.180
and then dropped me off at Arby's

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:43.013
and texted me and said,

00:10:43.013 --> 00:10:45.530
"Hope you learned from
our talk that we had."

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:50.530
And somebody paid for a
taxi from Lima to Finley,

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:54.640
which is an hour and 45 minutes away,

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.410
so I can get back home.

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:58.060
And that was the end of that,

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:01.020
but that's probably the hardest,

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:03.200
only because I knew my boyfriend,

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:05.150
I thought I was gonna die.

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:07.530
I'm smiling because I
don't know what else to do,

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:09.463
but yeah,

00:11:10.495 --> 00:11:11.906
I thought I was gonna die.

00:11:11.906 --> 00:11:13.729
That's the only time I really
thought I was gonna die.

